ection. I would mark this as a corrected premise rather than pretend detection capability.\\n\\nNext step: await researcher approval of this plan plus a decision on the \\\"What is Docta?\\\" clarification topic, then produce the full stage=result design (dataset spec, call-level workflow, controls, analysis plan, feasibility).\", \"evidence\": \"Inspected this turn (all commands run in the sandbox): (1) `ls -la /workspace` -> only task.json (363 bytes); its content: question text plus documents.track.md = \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\" (2) `find / -iname '*docta*'` (excluding /proc) -> empty. (3) `grep -ri docta /workspace /opt /usr/local /etc /srv /data` -> single hit: the question string in /workspace/task.json. (4) `python3 -c \\\"import docta\\\"` -> ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'docta'. (5) `pip3 show docta` -> WARNING: Package(s) not found. (6) `pip3 list` on Python 3.14.4 -> system packages only (ansible 13.1.0, Jinja2 3.1.6, cryptography 46.0.5, ...); no docta, no data-science packages; `importlib.util.find_spec` check confirmed pandas/numpy/sklearn/scipy/networkx/mlxtend all absent. (7) `/home/actor` empty; site-packages paths listed; no pip cache; no git repos found. (8) Environment metadata: network disabled, no datasets, cpu_affinity_count 224, gpu disabled. Repository observations relevant to design: none beyond task.json \\u2014 there is no Docta source, no example dataset, no evaluation utility to quote symbol names from.\", \"assumptions\": [\"ASSUMPTION (not inspected): 'Docta' refers to the QuantStack notebook-documentation tool (github.com/quantstack/docta) or the docta.ai PDF product; neither could be inspected here and no local source exists.\", \"ASSUMPTION (not inspected): Docta has NO tabular scoring/density/novelty/outlier/rule/cluster primitives; this is based on prior knowledge, not on anything found in this environment.\", \"ASSUMPTION: The eventual run environment (if this design is ever executed) could install Docta and scientific Python packages; the current sandbox cannot (network disabled, nothing preinstalled).\", \"FACT (inspected): /workspace contains only task.json; no dataset, no package, no evaluation utilities exist in this environment.\", \"FACT (inspected): the task is explicitly design-only per task.json ('repositories and compute are not required') and per the researcher's constraints.\", \"ASSUMPTION: 'Tabular dataset' means a CSV/parquet-style table with mixed numeric/categorical columns; the specific dataset is an open design choice pending researcher input.\", \"ASSUMPTION: No wall-clock/compute constraint matters for the design document itself beyond noting feasibility for a future execution.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"CRITICAL: The identity of 'Docta' and whether it has ANY capability relevant to rare-pattern detection is unresolved. The question's premise conflicts with the best-known tool of that name. Requires researcher clarification (repo/URL/pasted API, alternate tool confirmation, or the documentation-interpretation).\", \"Whether the intended deliverable expects detection to be done BY Docta (likely infeasible with the known tool) or a workflow DOCUMENTED BY Docta (coherent with the known tool).\", \"Whether a real dataset will be provided (datasets list is empty) or the design should specify a public/synthetic dataset with planted ground truth.\", \"If Docta turns out to be an obscure or internal package with analytics primitives, the whole method mapping would need rewriting once its API is visible.\"], \"summary\": \"Inspection finds no Docta anywhere; proposes clarification-first, controls-based design plan\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-639edb01-2789-4875-871f-621c18465ca6", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Inspection finds no Docta anywhere; proposes clarification-first, controls-based design plan", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
